# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch J."""
DESC_J = {
    "PT": {
        94: "A member of Kazuki's delinquent gang, which was at odds with Kappei.\nWhile evacuating together with Kazuki and the others, he was captured by the Gaizock and, without his knowledge, converted into a human bomb.",
        95: "A member of Kappei's self-proclaimed honor guard, nicknamed the 'Plain Pair.' She is 12 years old.\nHer family was caught in a Gaizock attack, and her mother suffered severe injuries. Believing the Jin family was to blame, Aki vented her fierce anger at Kappei. Deep down, though, she understood that Kappei and the others were not truly at fault, and with her mother's encouragement she gradually reconciled with him.\nShe was later captured by the Gaizock, but Kappei rescued her.",
        96: "Another member of Kappei's self-proclaimed honor guard, one of the so-called 'Plain Pair.'\nHer family was likewise caught in a Gaizock attack, and, convinced that the Jin family was responsible, she directed her anger at Kappei.\nLike Aki, she was captured by the Gaizock, but Kazuki rescued her before she could be turned into a human bomb, and she narrowly managed to escape.",
        97: "Captain of the Bandock and commander of the Gaizock, a cyborg whose body has been replaced almost entirely with machinery.\nOriginally from a planet on the frontier, he became a servant of the Gaizock god (Computer Doll No. 8) and, on its orders, schemes to exterminate humanity.\nCruel by nature and fond of slaughter, he carries out one atrocity after another, including the human bomb operations, while at the same time showing a strong interest in Earth's culture and entertainment.\nThe object of his interest changes constantly - having a designer tailor him outfits, indulging in pachinko, sunbathing, or belting out songs with a band - producing a comical side wildly out of balance with his ruthlessness.",
        98: "A weapons officer of the Gaizock.\nA schemer who proposes various attacks to Butcher. He also has a foolish streak, however - on one occasion his hand slipped while trying to press a missile launch switch, setting off a human bomb and blowing himself up.",
        99: "An operations officer of the Gaizock, in charge of command at the front lines.\nHis large build and a face crossed with countless scars give him a formidable, intimidating look, but he shows absolute obedience to Butcher's orders.\nConfident but not much of a strategist, he sometimes cornered Zambot 3 only to let victory slip away at the crucial moment.",
        100: "The electronic brain at the core of the Bandock, and the true body of the Gaizock.\nIt had ceased activity after destroying the planet Vier 200 years earlier. Upon approaching Earth's sphere, it reactivated its programming and ordered Butcher to annihilate the human race.",
        101: "The pilot of Daitarn 3, known everywhere by his nickname, 'Banjo Haran, the Talk of the Town.' He is 18 years old.\nCheerful and upbeat, brimming with humor, and never without a joke even in a crisis, he is a man others can rely on. That he never comes across as smug despite his flashy, self-assured manner is thanks to the very human side he lets show from time to time.\nHis physical abilities are outstanding, allowing him to hold his own against Meganoids even unarmed. His prowess is so great that rumors occasionally circulate that Banjo himself might be a Meganoid.\nHe harbors fierce hatred for the Meganoids, and for his father, who created them and used Banjo's brother and mother as test subjects. He is ruthless enough to accept the sacrifice of his comrades if it means destroying the Meganoids, yet his friends still place absolute trust and affection in him regardless.\nNote that the 'Haran Conglomerate,' which recurred throughout the older Super Robot Wars titles, is an original setting created for the games; in the anime itself, he is simply established as extremely wealthy.",
        102: "The butler in service to Banjo. Age 55.\nFrom attending to Banjo's daily needs, to preparing meals and maintaining various machines, to even sortieing in Daitarn 3 itself, he handles every task flawlessly - a butler among butlers.\nNothing is known of his background or past history, but his great skill and character have earned him the complete trust of Banjo and the others.\nHe is also a first-rate marksman - so much so, by his own account, that people used to say, \"Wyatt Earp or Garrison?\"",
        103: "Banjo's assistant. Age 17.\nOriginally a student at the Interpol Academy, she met Banjo while investigating a Meganoid incident and has traveled with him ever since.\nBefitting her Interpol background, she is a cool, dependable, and intelligent beauty well versed in handling firearms and piloting machinery. When it comes to Banjo, however, she is not above clashing with Beauty, and it is not unusual to see her sink to the same level as her rival.",
        104: "Banjo's little brother figure, a mischievous boy who calls himself the 'first assistant.' Age 10.\nHe lost his parents to the Meganoids. After meeting Banjo and fighting alongside him, he ended up staying on as a freeloader at the Haran mansion.\nHe is known for his 'hot-blooded fireball' personality and for having, as he puts it, 'a great big dream.'",
        105: "Banjo's assistant. Age 17.\nThe pampered daughter of the president of Beauty Tourism, she lived a life free of want, but volunteered to become Banjo's assistant to see for herself whether the famous Banjo Haran lived up to his reputation.\nShe is beautiful enough to have won the 'Miss Inter-Beauty' pageant and has an outstanding figure to match. Her personality, however, is extremely childish - she clashes with Reika over Banjo, and, being close to him in mental age, gets into genuine fights with Toppo.",
        106: "A Civilian boy who single-mindedly pushes forward, true to his own convictions. He is 16 years old.\nHe broke the 'Three-Day Law' set down by the Innocents, which held that any crime became void after three days had passed, and kept pursuing Timp, the man who killed his parents. Along the way he met Rag and the others, and the group tried together to steal a Xabungle they happened to spot. They ultimately failed, but circumstances afterward led him to come aboard the Iron Gear.\nHe is filled with a drive that goes well beyond mere initiative, and once he sets his mind on something he pushes forward no matter what. On the surface it looks like nothing but recklessness, but that very attitude embodied the 'strong Civilian' the Innocents had longed for across generations. His influence spread to others dissatisfied with the status quo, and he ultimately struck down Cashim King, the root of all the trouble.\nHe is quite skilled at piloting Walker Machines, and even taught Blume and the others at one point. That said, his teaching covered only the basics - he seems to have relied more on brute force than fine technique to get through most situations.\nWith his round face, easygoing manner, and rough, thoughtless personality, he would not seem, by ordinary standards, to be popular with girls. And yet, perhaps because he was unconventional in every respect, he was quite popular with the girls around him.",
        107: "Captain of the Iron Gear. Age 16. Her father, the trading merchant Carrying Cargo, died in battle, leaving her to inherit his position against her own wishes.\nShe admires the cultural life of the Innocents and dreams of bringing a flowering of culture to the surface world. She herself, though, can hardly be called ladylike - she is quick-tempered and handy with a throwing knife, more tomboy than lady. Even so, she seems to be quite self-conscious about her personality deep down.\nShe eventually falls for the unconventional Jiron and finds herself locked in rivalry with Rag over him.",
        108: "Helmsman and mechanic of the Iron Gear.\nA rather nagging, short-tempered man, always shouting, his outbursts were so much like hysterics that people called him 'Mr. Hysterics.'\nHe has a deep love for machines and absolute confidence in his skill at maintaining and handling them. He has also been quietly collecting blueprints for the machines purchased from the Innocents, secretly harboring the ambition of one day building machines with his own hands without relying on the Innocents.",
        109: "Elche's loyal servant and bodyguard.\nHe was once worked like a slave under the corrupt Lockman Gillan, until Elche bought his freedom. He has sworn absolute loyalty to her ever since.\nHis basic physical abilities are extremely high, from the tremendous strength his muscular frame can unleash to his surprising nimbleness. When Elche is in danger, his abilities power up even further, and he displays superhuman strength.",
        110: "The female leader of the bandit gang Sand Rat.\nWhile attacking a group of Lockmen, she got help from Jiron, who collapsed nearby, and the two hit it off. Lending him a hand in stealing his Xabungle drew her into the affairs of the Cargo family, and eventually her whole team was hired on aboard the Iron Gear.\nWith a temperament, nerve, and drive that put most men to shame, she is skilled not only at piloting Walker Machines but also at commanding the Iron Gear whenever Elche is absent.\nShe falls easily for anyone who treats her like a lady, Jiron chief among them. She even joined the self-styled 'Arthur Honor Guard,' though Jiron remained her true favorite.",
        111: "A member of the bandit gang Sand Rat. Age 15.\nA quick-draw expert and a wisecracking cynic, he plays it cool but is kind at heart, hiding a passionate spirit.\nHe acts as something of a sub-leader among the members. In truth he is in love with Rag, and resents how attached she has become to the newcomer Jiron - a grudge that once drove him to leave the Iron Gear.",
        112: "A member of the bandit gang Sand Rat. Age 16.\nGentle and honest, kind-hearted yet strong, considerate and full of compassion - a rare and valuable presence aboard the Iron Gear, where so many others have fiery tempers.\nSkilled with firearms, he handles every job imaginable: piloting and maintaining Walker Machines, and serving as both helmsman and gunner aboard the Iron Gear. Despite all this, he never once got a moment in the spotlight - a fact summed up perfectly by his own line, \"That's because I'm a side character.\" He seems to understand his own role perfectly well, which may make him the most emotionally mature person in the entire cast.",
        113: "A member of the bandit gang Sand Rat.\nShe carries a little bear-shaped pouch and serves as something of a team mascot, but handles her work with real professional skill. She often rides along with Jiron in the Xabungle or Walker Gallier to provide support.\nHer sharp remarks about other people's psychology hint at real depth of insight and a maturity beyond her years. Even so, she cries and screams like any child her age when things get dangerous.\nIn Jiron's words, she will \"grow up to be quite a woman.\"",
        114: "A member of the Iron Gear crew. Age 15.\nShe was once a member of the anti-Innocent organization 'Salt,' but gave up on their leader Katakam out of frustration with his ineffectiveness, and, agreeing with Jiron's views, ended up where she is now.\nHer active personality suits her for reconnaissance and intelligence work using a small Walker Machine called the Leg, which she carried out energetically.\nShe and Maria have fought together aboard a captured Doran, and the two seem to get along well in general, including forming the self-styled 'Arthur Honor Guard' together and generally having fun.",
        115: "A girl who gathered orphans together and ran a self-sufficient farm.\nA thoroughgoing pacifist. Taking care of others is considered eccentric behavior on Zora, and Rag did in fact call her a strange one. After meeting Jiron and recognizing her own naivety, she cut off her long hair as a way of atoning for it.\nShe later joined 'Salt' as an assistant to Medic. After reuniting with Jiron and the others, she began taking up a gun herself and joining the fighting.\nAfter Arthur's appearance, she became a huge fan of his along with Rag and Birin, squealing with excitement over him like any ordinary girl.",
        116: "A wandering Civilian doctor.\nA heavy drinker, but a reliable physician. At the outset he treated Jiron's arm and even gave him clothes, only to have the payment for it stolen by Rag, effectively leaving him stiffed for his trouble.\nHe later passed through 'Salt' before coming aboard the Iron Gear, where he served afterward as Jiron's strategic advisor. He is a man of considerable intelligence, at times making remarks that seem to see straight through the Innocents' intentions.",
        117: "The Breaker who killed Jiron's parents. He seemed at first to be a mere drifter, but he is in fact an agent of the Innocents, whose job is to pit Civilians against each other under the guise of 'trials.'\nHis cunning, his skill piloting Walker Machines, and his quick-draw marksmanship are all first-rate, and his manner carries the air of a truly formidable figure. Yet he has a slightly bumbling side too, and provided plenty of comic moments, such as burning his nose on the cigar clenched in his teeth.\nHe fought Jiron again and again as Jiron pursued him to avenge his parents, and when it finally seemed he had been defeated, he once got himself out of danger by playing dead.",
        118: "A Breaker acting as an agent of the Innocents.\nHe was once the leader of the Breakers employed by Carrying Cargo, but Jiron's arrival threw everything into chaos and cost him his position.\nFrom then on he devoted himself entirely to scheming toward two goals: defeating Jiron, and winning over Elche, whose affections he continued to pursue despite her rejection.\nWhen he first appeared he came across as cool-headed and sharp, but he grew increasingly sloppy as time went on. By the latter half of the story, it had become a running gag for him to take his failures out on his partner Geraba.",
        119: "Hora's subordinate, partner, and little brother figure.\nTough-looking and strong in a fight, he is also no slouch at piloting Walker Machines. Surprisingly timid at heart, though, he cannot bring himself to defy Hora, having been beaten by him once before.\nHe once pulled off the bold feat of infiltrating the Iron Gear by pretending to have given up on Hora, then kidnapping Elche. The acting skill he showed off in the process makes one wonder whether he could not, in fact, stand on his own without Hora.",
        120: "Wife of the courier Karasu Karasu.\nThe sex appeal radiating from her overly voluptuous figure is intense enough to overwhelm even Jiron, and more than a few Breakers have fallen prey to her deep, lingering thank-you kisses.\nWhen she was shot down during an attack on the Iron Gear, her husband, believing her dead, launched a war of vengeance - only to be beaten back himself. Through this convoluted turn of events, she ended up being the one avenging her husband instead, and has relentlessly pursued the Iron Gear ever since.",
        121: "The supreme ruler of the Innocents. Age 17. His name is a hereditary title, not his actual birth name.\nBetrayed by his close aide Cashim, he was imprisoned at Yopp Point until Jiron and the others rescued him. He then declared to all the Innocents that Cashim must be overthrown.\nInnocents cannot survive for long in the open air, and it is this frailty, along with his innocent nature and above all his beauty, that has captivated Rag, Birin, and Maria.",
        122: "A Newtype boy who joins the AEUG, and the pilot of the Z Gundam. He is 17 years old.\nOriginally an ordinary, if somewhat sensitive, high school student on the space colony 'Green Noa.' He has a complex about his feminine-sounding name, Kamille, which led him to throw himself into more masculine hobbies like the Homo Avis (a simple hang glider) and karate. Perhaps thanks to having parents who were technical officers in the Federation Forces, he is also well versed in machinery himself, skilled enough to win the Jr. Mobile Suit tournament.\nWhen Jerid mocked his name and the two came to blows, however, he found himself at odds with the Titans. Circumstances led him to help Quattro steal the Gundam Mk-II, and he ended up joining the AEUG outright. Through combat he awakened to his abilities as a Newtype, and gradually rose to become one of the AEUG's ace pilots.\nAt first he simply fought out of resentment toward the Titans, but through his encounters and partings with adults like Quattro and Amuro, and with women like Four and Rosamia, he grew tremendously as a person. In time, while searching for a way to end the war, he came to fly through space guided by his own will.",
        123: "One of the central figures who laid the foundations of the AEUG. His rank is captain. He is 27 years old.\nA man of many mysteries, who wears sunglasses that hide his true face. His true identity is Char Aznable, the Red Comet of the Principality of Zeon forces, who went missing after the end of the One Year War.\nIncidentally, Quattro is Italian for the number '4', marking it as the fourth name he has used - after his birth name, Casval, his Earth alias, Edwau, and his Zeon alias, Char.\nAt first he made use of his outstanding mobile suit piloting skill, fighting on the front lines aboard the Rick Dias and the Hyaku Shiki. But his reunion with Amuro, along with the assassination of Brigadier General Blex, the AEUG's representative, led him to step into the spotlight as a political leader.",
        124: "The ace pilot of Karaba. His rank is captain. He is 24 years old.\nA man who fought through the One Year War in the RX-78 Gundam and has since become something of a legend. After the war, however, he came to be seen as a threat and was kept under Federation surveillance, left to languish in an unimportant post on Earth. By this time he had lost nearly all his will to fight - partly due to the oppressive environment, but mostly because of the trauma left by his encounter and parting with Lalah Sune.\nA sudden visit from Fraw, Katz, and their family, however, prompted him to resolve to stand up and fight again. After deserting and joining up with Karaba, he began working alongside his old rival Char and the youthful Kamille. As the fighting continued, he regained his old instincts, and, piloting the Rick Dias and later the Dijeh, became a core fighting force for Karaba.",
        125: "Captain of the AEUG cruiser Argama. His rank is lieutenant colonel.\nDuring the One Year War, though only an officer cadet, circumstances placed him in command of the White Base, which he saw through to the end of the war. His distinguished performance, however, made him a figure the top brass viewed with suspicion, and after the war he was shunted into the unimportant post of captain of the liaison shuttle 'Temptation.'\nHarboring doubts about the self-righteous methods of the Titans, he accepted Quattro's invitation and decided to join the AEUG.\nDrawing on the experience he built up during the One Year War, his sound command has led to numerous victories.",
        126: "A bridge crewman of the Argama, serving with the AEUG.\nA cheerful, easygoing sort. His main duties are the ship's navigation, communications, and sensor tracking, and he gets along well with Saegusa, who sits next to him and handles much the same role.\nIn the TV version he often hung around with Kamille as well, and once teased him into a fight that got him sent to detention.",
        127: "A bridge crewman of the Argama.\nHis main duties are the ship's navigation and helm, and he gets along well with Torres, who sits next to him and handles much the same role.",
        128: "Once a member of the Titans, she defected to the AEUG after witnessing Basque's despicable tactics firsthand. Her rank remains lieutenant.\nHer outstanding piloting skill was apparently valued in the AEUG as well, and she was entrusted with mainstay machines such as the Rick Dias, the Gundam Mk-II, and the Super Gundam, all of which she handled with ease.\nShe has a strong will that acts on her own convictions, along with the sternness of a soldier. At the same time, she also carries a feminine gentleness. She always kept up a cold front toward Henken's advances, but in truth she does not seem to have minded them all that much.",
        129: "An officer of the Titans. Her rank is lieutenant. She is 24 years old.\nHer mobile suit piloting skill is high enough that she was selected as a pilot for the Gundam Mk-II despite being a woman.\nAmid the many Titans who hold to an elitist, chosen-people ideology, she is one of the few with any real sense of decency, and this leads her to feel disgust at Basque's ruthless, by-any-means tactics.",
        130: "A member of the AEUG, with the rank of ensign. She is 23 years old.\nShe lost her parents during the One Year War and spent time taking part in guerrilla activity in North America. Having grown up amid fighting, she is a brave soldier who readily volunteers even for spy missions with death constantly at hand. At the same time, though, she longed for a man who could be a source of emotional support.",
        131: "A former member of the AEUG, now an officer of the Titans. Her rank is ensign.\nShe sought comfort in Quattro, but his attitude and words made her realize she was not needed by him, leaving her disillusioned. While on a mission she then met Scirocco, and, drawn to him, defected to the Titans.\nFrom that point on she no longer carried out spy work as she had with the AEUG, devoting herself instead to piloting the Pallas Athene.",
        132: "A subordinate of Quattro's who joins the AEUG. His rank is lieutenant.\nHe formerly belonged to the old Principality of Zeon forces and took part in the One Year War as well. He is one of the few veteran pilots aboard the Argama, and a good senior figure to Kamille.\nHe is deeply trusted by Quattro, and has at times taken command of the mobile suit corps in his place.",
        133: "A subordinate of Quattro's who joins the AEUG. His rank is lieutenant.\nHe formerly belonged to the old Principality of Zeon forces and took part in the One Year War as well. He is one of the few veteran pilots aboard the Argama, and a good senior figure to Kamille.\nHe and Apolly are comrades who have survived countless brushes with death together, and the two are often found acting side by side.",
        134: "Kamille's childhood friend, age 17. Her name, written in kanji, would be 'Hanazono Rei.'\nBecause she was known to be an acquaintance of Kamille, who stole the Gundam Mk-II, she and her parents were captured by Basque. After Bright rescued her, she joined the AEUG - partly out of defiance toward the Titans - and volunteered as a pilot. Though troubled by her own lack of skill, she fought her way through the entire Gryps War.\nShe has a fussy, caretaking personality and has long kept after Kamille about his everyday habits and manners. Kamille, for his part, seems to have found her nagging rather tiresome deep down. Perhaps because of her personality, she also became the one responsible for looking after Shinta and Kum, the children Quattro brought aboard the Argama.",
        135: "A boy soldier who joins the AEUG.\nHaving come aboard the White Base as a refugee during the One Year War, he was raised after the war as the adopted son of Hayato and Fraw. When the family visited Amuro, however, he volunteered on his own to join the AEUG, and joined up with Amuro aboard the Audomura.\nA complete change from his quiet childhood self, he has grown into a reckless, hot-blooded young man. He harbors rivalry toward Kamille, who is close to him in age, and shows a boyish immaturity - launching without authorization, ignoring orders, and falling for Sara, whom he met on the battlefield.",
        136: "An officer of the Titans, with the rank of lieutenant. He is 24 years old.\nHighly elitist by nature, he secretly harbors ambitions of seizing control of the Titans.\nSelected as a pilot for the Gundam Mk-II alongside Kacricon and Emma, he had been enjoying smooth sailing as a soldier's career. His encounter with Kamille, however, threw his fate badly off course.\nAt first he was unfamiliar with mobile suit piloting, crash-landing the Gundam Mk-II and standing no chance at all against Quattro. But fueled in part by his personal grudge against Kamille, he steadily improved, gradually drawing the attention of both Jamitov and Scirocco. He then went through one new machine after another - the Marasai, the Gabthley, the Byarlant, the Baund Doc - relentlessly pursuing Kamille all the while.",
        137: "An officer of the Titans, with the rank of lieutenant. He is 24 years old.\nHe was selected as a pilot for the Gundam Mk-II alongside Jerid and Emma. He gets along well with his colleague Jerid and the two are nearly always together.\nBesides being a skilled mobile suit pilot, he is also sharp-minded, the scheming, strategist type.\nHe apparently had a girlfriend on Earth named Amelia.",
        138: "A pilot of the Galbady Beta assigned to the Titans cruiser 'Bosnie.' Her rank is captain.\nDespite being a woman, her piloting skill is such that she commands the Galbady squadron. Blunt-spoken and combative by nature, she made no effort to hide her rivalry with the blatantly elitist Jerid, dismissing him outright as a \"soft little boy.\"",
        139: "A member of the Titans who serves as both captain of the Garuda and pilot of the Asshimar. His rank is major.\nExcellent both as a commander and a pilot, he is deeply trusted by his subordinates. His arrogant, overbearing manner is simply the expression of a confidence backed by real ability.\nHe detests the instability of Enhanced Humans, and seems to have found the newly assigned Rosamia an unwelcome presence as well.\nTasked with hunting down the Audomura, he pursued Kamille and the others relentlessly, time after time.",
        140: "Bran's adjutant, who takes command of the Garuda's combat operations whenever Bran sorties.\nAfter Bran's death, he took over as captain of the Garuda and tried to avenge Bran using Four's Psycho Gundam, though he seems to have remained skeptical of the very existence of Enhanced Humans.",
    },
}
